    <briefdescription>
<para>REST controller for managing staff membership of service entities. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A {serviceType} path segment selects a <ref refid="classStaffController" kindref="compound">StaffController&lt;T&gt;</ref> from a variant registry (clinics, pharmacies, laboratories, radiologycenters). Handlers use the shared callback pattern to map controller status codes to JSON HTTP responses, build a <ref refid="structRequester" kindref="compound">Requester</ref> from Auth attributes, and run async coroutines or the DbExecutor-backed dispatch according to DatabaseConfig::async. All routes are SECURE. Controllers and the executor are shared service-locator objects. <simplesect kind="note"><para>Drogon prepends its controller path (/api/v2/staff) to the METHOD_ADD paths below, so the effective URLs contain a doubled &quot;staff&quot; segment (e.g. /api/v2/staff/.../staff/invite). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
